Firmware lineage
----------------

GOGUFW is based directly on Armel / F4HWN Fusion for the Quansheng UV-K1 and
UV-K5 V3. The current platform and official multiboot implementation derive
from the joint UV-K1/PY32F071 work of Armel / F4HWN and muzkr:

  https://github.com/armel/uv-k1-k5v3-firmware-custom
  https://github.com/muzkr/uv-k1-k5v3-firmware-custom

Armel / F4HWN also created the original RF Log feature. GOGUFW's RF Log Lite
was inspired by that work and independently reimplemented as a compact,
20-entry, RAM-only activity log for the more constrained GOGUFW build.

That work builds on the wider UV-K5 open-firmware lineage:

  Dual Tachyon - original open UV-K5 firmware and hardware drivers
  https://github.com/DualTachyon/uv-k5-firmware

  OneOfEleven - custom radio features, AM-fix and scrambler foundations
  https://github.com/OneOfEleven/uv-k5-firmware-custom

  fagci - original Spectrum Analyzer implementation
  https://github.com/fagci/uv-k5-firmware-fagci-mod

  egzumer - integrated custom-firmware base and extended feature set
  https://github.com/egzumer/uv-k5-firmware-custom

The F4HWN base also contains optimization, FM/UI/Spectrum and hardware-support
work by mrkusypl and Tunas1337, among many other upstream contributors:

  https://github.com/mrkusypl/uv-k1-k5v3-firmware-custom
  https://github.com/Tunas1337

Feature-specific attribution
----------------------------

GOGUFW Messenger uses its own packet format, persistent storage, UI,
wake-preamble behavior, ACK/retry logic and multi-radio Range Check protocol.
Its BK4829 RF implementation adapts the AirCopy/FSK facilities inherited from
the Dual Tachyon/egzumer/F4HWN codebase.

Earlier radio-to-radio Messenger implementations by joaquimorg and Kamil / NUNU
helped establish the feature on the UV-K5 family and served as comparison
references. NUNU's manual Spectrum behavior also served as a design reference
while correcting GOGUFW's manual Spectrum mode:

  https://github.com/joaquimorg/UV-KX-firmware
  https://github.com/kamilsss655/uv-k5-firmware-custom

The GOGUFW-specific Messenger, HEARD, multi-radio Range Check, CALLTX feature
and melodies, named FM memories, Live RSSI control, channel policies, UI
adaptations and matching CHIRP support were developed by Gökhan Günalp /
Gogu-Qs. CALLTX uses the inherited low-level tone-generator and TX audio path,
but its feature design, melodies, selection/preview behavior and user interface
are GOGUFW work.

